ke the perfect  opportunity to just throw storm in there  and there may have already been a little  hint at that in the trailer now in  storm's original backstory she is a  descendant from a long line of african  witch priestesses with white hair and  blue eyes and a natural gift for sorcery  well in the black panther wakanda  forever teaser trailer that we got we  can actually see that some people in the  teaser trailer during the ceremony for  t'challa have white hair perhaps this  person could be from the same tribe that  storm's mother was from and storm's  mother was actually the princess of the  tribe perhaps this is a hint that some  other tribes that storm might be from  could show up to the funeral now i would  love for them to kind of hit the nail on  the head and just straight up say this  is storm this is aurora but i think  marvel studios might be a little bit  more subtle just having a woman show up  with white hair saying something along  the lines of i'll miss you friend and  just hint at it and maybe not address  her by name but i do really hope that  this could be a cameo that we could get  and again based off of the story in the  comics and the future of the mcu  introducing the mutants and the x-men i  think it's a perfect opportunity now i  do also think that neymar is going to  show up for the funeral neymar and  wakanda have a very long history with  each other and they're not always  enemies namor isn't really a villain  he's more of an anti-hero but given the  long history between wakanda and  atlantis and the comics i'm sure that's  going to somewhat transfer over to the  mcu i'm sure wakanda and the atlanteans  aren't just going to go to war with each  other randomly or after their first  meeting i'm sure they've met before in  the mcu in fact in the trailer we saw  namor as a kid on land it could have  been in wakanda so i'm sure they have a  relationship already and since the  atlanteans are kind of like the  wakandans they try to stay secretive  they seclude themselves from the world  and of course they live underwater i'm  sure they've shared many things in  common including vibranium that is  probably in the ocean i'm assuming that  namor has probably met king t'challa  even if he met him before he was king  and i actually think this could be the  first time we see him in the film in the  beginning at the funeral he shows up to  pay his respect but i'm sure it's going  to be somewhat controversial because of  the history between wakanda and atlantis  this is probably going to be where the  tension starts namor shows up for the  funeral wakandans don't really like that  and then something else happens and the  two of them just go to war with each  other now like i mentioned before  there's a rumor going around that dr  doom could actually be behind everything  that happens in wakanda forever because  he wants to start a war between atlantis  and wakanda so he himself can get some  vibranium now having said that i don't  think we're actually going to see doom  in the movie i think we'll probably hear  a name drop or perhaps he'll show up in  a post-credits scene but i would  absolutely freak out if victor von doom  showed up for the funeral of t'challa i  do not think this is going to happen but  the possibilities for a ton of cameos  are very very real so i am definitely  expecting some cameos we'll have to see  who it is but i am really hoping for  storm it just makes sense but hey let me  know your thoughts about this in the  comments down below if you love marvel  don't forget to subscribe so you can  stay up to date on all the latest news  for live updates you can follow me on  instagram and twitter and as always  thank you all so much for watching woof  you

